        "original_id": "1473573c-e87d-5760-ac0d-1dbf7315005e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William H. Masters, Virginia E. Johnson\n- Organizations: Masters and Johnson research team\n- Concepts: orgasmic platform, sensate focusing, human sexual response, sexual disorders and dysfunctions\n\nFacts:\n- From 1957 until the 1990s, the Masters and Johnson research team was composed of William H. Masters and Virginia E. Johnson.\n- From 1957 until the 1990s, the Masters and Johnson research team pioneered research into human sexual response and the diagnosis and treatment of sexual disorders and dysfunctions.\n- Masters and Johnson introduced the term sensate focusing.\n- Sensate focusing was aimed at increasing personal and interpersonal awareness of one’s own needs and another person’s needs.\n- Masters and Johnson labeled the orgasmic platform as the tissues of the outer third of the vagina.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
